{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"goai-litsearch","tool":"save_to_library","arguments":{"papers_json":"[{"id":"1506.07142","title":"Effects of sublattice symmetry and frustration on ionic transport in garnet solid electrolytes","authors":["Boris Kozinsky","Sneha A. Akhade","Pierre Hirel","Adham Hashibon","Christian Elsässer","Prateek Mehta","Alan Logeat","Ulrich Eisele"],"year":2015,"venue":"arXiv","doi":"10.1103/physrevlett.116.055901","arxiv_id":"1506.07142","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.07142","pdf_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1506.07142","abstract":"We use rigorous group-theoretic techniques and molecular dynamics to investigate the connection between structural symmetry and ionic conductivity in the garnet family of solid Li-ion electrolytes. We identify new ordered phases and order-disorder phase transitions that are relevant for conductivity optimization. Ionic transport in this materials family is controlled by the frustration of the Li sublattice caused by incommensurability with the host structure at non-integer Li concentrations, while ordered phases explain regions of sharply lower conductivity. Disorder is therefore predicted to be optimal for ionic transport in this and other conductor families with strong Li interaction.","citation_count":null,"publication_type":"preprint","sources":["arxiv"]},{"id":"1902.06831","title":"Ionic conductivity enhacements and low temperature synthesis of Li7La3Zr2O12 garnets by Bi aliovalent substitutions","authors":["Derek K. Schwanz","Andres Villa","Mahalingam Balasubramanian","Benjamin Helfrecht","Ernesto E. Marinero"],"year":2019,"venue":"arXiv","doi":null,"arxiv_id":"1902.06831","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1902.06831","pdf_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1902.06831","abstract":"We report on a novel approach to synthesize cubic-phase fast ionic conducting garnet-type solid state electrolytes based on Bi doped Li7La3Zr2O12 (LLZO). Bi aliovalent substitution into LLZO utilizing the Pechini processing method is successfully employed to synthesize Li7-xLa3Zr2-xBixO12 compounds. Ionic conductivities up to 2.0 x 10-4 S/cm are achieved in structures not fully densified. Cubic phase Li6La3ZrBiO12 powders are generated in the temperature range from 650 °C to 900 °C in air. In contrast, in the absence of Bi and under identical synthesis conditions, the cubic garnet phase of Li7La3Zr2O12 is not formed below 700 °C while a transformation to the tetragonal phase is observed at 900 °C for the un-doped compound. The critical role of Bi in lowering the formation temperature of the cubic phase and improvements in ionic conductivity is investigated through microstructural studies and AC impedance measurements.","citation_count":null,"publication_type":"preprint","sources":["arxiv"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.ssi.2017.11.005","title":"On processing-structure-property relations and high ionic conductivity in garnet-type Li5La3Ta2O12 solid electrolyte thin films grown by CO2-laser assisted CVD","authors":["Christoph Loho","Ruzica Djenadic","Paul Mundt","Oliver Clemens","Horst Hahn"],"year":2017,"venue":"Solid State Ionics","doi":"10.1016/j.ssi.2017.11.005","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssi.2017.11.005","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":21,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1515/nano.11671_2015.129","title":"Lithium ionic conduction and relaxation dynamics of spark plasma sintered Li5La3Ta2O12 garnet nanoceramics","authors":["Mohamad M Ahmad"],"year":2016,"venue":"nano Online","doi":"10.1515/nano.11671_2015.129","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1515/nano.11671_2015.129","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":0,"publication_type":"dataset","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.ssi.2014.01.046","title":"Preparation and electrical properties of garnet-type Li6BaLa2Ta2O12 lithium solid electrolyte thin films prepared by pulsed laser deposition","authors":["Jochen Reinacher","Stefan Berendts","Jürgen Janek"],"year":2014,"venue":"Solid State Ionics","doi":"10.1016/j.ssi.2014.01.046","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssi.2014.01.046","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":54,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2017.08.109","title":"Evidence of the chemical stability of the garnet-type solid electrolyte Li5La3Ta2O12 towards lithium by a surface science approach","authors":["Mathias Fingerle","Christoph Loho","Thimo Ferber","Horst Hahn","René Hausbrand"],"year":2017,"venue":"Journal of Power Sources","doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2017.08.109","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpowsour.2017.08.109","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":33,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.ceramint.2018.02.118","title":"Enhancement of density and ionic conductivity for garnet-type Li5La3Ta2O12 solid electrolyte by self-consolidation strategy","authors":["Pengcheng Zhao","Yu Xiang","Yan Xu","Yuehua Wen","Wenfeng Zhang","Xiayu Zhu","Meng Li","Zhaoqing Jin","Hai Ming","Gaoping Cao"],"year":2018,"venue":"Ceramics International","doi":"10.1016/j.ceramint.2018.02.118","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ceramint.2018.02.118","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":11,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1007/s10854-015-3473-6","title":"Concentration and mobility of mobile Li+ ions in Li6BaLa2Ta2O12 and Li5La3Ta2O12 garnet lithium ion conductors","authors":["Mohamad M. Ahmad","Abdullah Al-Jaafari"],"year":2015,"venue":"Journal of Materials Science: Materials in Electronics","doi":"10.1007/s10854-015-3473-6","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10854-015-3473-6","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":7,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.ceramint.2018.01.065","title":"Structure and ionic conductivity of Li7La3Zr2−xGexO1